{ singledispatch

 `singledispatch` allows for a rudimentary function overloading:
code {
from functools import singledispatch

@singledispatch
def F(a):
    print('F was called')

# Overload F for an int
@F.register(int)
def _(a):
    print('F was called, the argument is an int')

# Overload F for a str
@F.register(str)
def _(a):
    print('F was called, the argument is a str')

F([])
F(42)
F('Hello world')
code }

  See also PEP 443, PEP 3124 and `pkgutil.simplegeneric`.

